# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore - backend/auth-service (Hospital Management System)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose: keep the Docker build context lean and secure. Everything listed
# here is excluded from the context sent to the daemon, so it can never be
# COPYed into the image. This trims image size and build time and, critically,
# prevents host secrets and local installs from being baked into a layer.
#
# Build-context note: the auth-service Dockerfile is designed for a
# REPOSITORY-ROOT build context (so the npm workspace root and backend/shared
# are available for `npm ci`). Docker reads the .dockerignore at the ROOT of
# the build context, so the canonical excludes ideally also live at the repo
# root. This service-level file is still provided because it is the standard
# companion convention, it is honored by BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore
# (Dockerfile.dockerignore) and for any service-context build, and it documents
# intent. Patterns are kept generic and path-relative so they stay meaningful
# regardless of which directory is the context root.
#
# Ordering matters: like .gitignore, a later pattern overrides an earlier one,
# so a negation such as `!.env.example` MUST appear after the `.env.*` rule
# that would otherwise exclude it. Do NOT add patterns that would exclude
# `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `src/`; they are required to build
# and run the service. Runtime configuration is injected via the container
# environment, never a baked-in file.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Dependencies (installed inside the image via `npm ci`, never copied) ----
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# ---- Environment & secrets (NEVER bake secrets into an image) ----
.env
.env.*
# Keep the committed, secret-free template (re-included after the .env.* rule).
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---- Tests & coverage (not needed at runtime) ----
tests/
**/tests/
coverage/
**/coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ---- Logs & temp ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
logs/
tmp/
temp/

# ---- VCS & CI ----
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# ---- Editor / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# ---- Docker meta (build files do not belong inside the context/image) ----
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore

# ---- Docs (optional; keep the image small) ----
*.md
**/*.md
